# Project change rules

Context: Applied AI Lab static website (HTML, CSS, vanilla JS), plus a Python newsletter tool in ai_brief/. Work through the tasks I paste next, one at a time.

Rules for every task:
- Do NOT modify, rename, move, resize, recompress or re-reference any image, logo, GIF or the images_icons/ folder, and don't change any <img> markup or image URLs in data files. Assume all images exist.
- Create a branch first (audit/cleanup). Make one commit per task with a clear message.
- Before deleting or renaming any file, search the whole repo (HTML, CSS, JS, JSON, README) for references to it, and list what you found.
- Before and after each task, check these pages at 360px, 768px, 1024px and 1440px wide, in BOTH light and dark mode: index, fellowship, event, ai-insights, industry, 404. Report any visual difference you did not intend.
- Do not change visible design or copy unless the task says to. If something is ambiguous, stop and ask me.
- At the end of each task, give me a short list of what changed and anything you chose not to do.